    "body": "Yes, EXIF is really only present in images produced from camera/scan devices, which is why it's there in JPEG.  However, you won't (normally) see it in PNG (it wasn't added to the standard till 2017, http://ftp-osl.osuosl.org/pub/libpng/documents/pngext-1.5.0.html#C.eXIf), and its not part of newer image formats like AV1.  You certainly won't see it in video, audio or documents.",
